{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "scope": "scsp-synth-code-allocation-physical-channel-navigation",
  "baseCommit": "18a9bc47294d3255e977858e9d1e93beca674d27",
  "review": "Native CH member buttons navigate through the existing physical channel selection callback from the detached Synth / Code allocation view. Navigation preserves allocator ownership and saved A–F mapping, source operator, keyboard target policy, logical Code lanes, running Code and detached drafts; unavailable, hidden, disposed and changed-during-gesture targets cannot navigate. The pure allocation description and its helpers remain byte-identical. Complete reviewed UI and proof-hook predecessors restore exactly to the base commit before the existing calibration chain. Channel selector implementation, allocation/instrument/routing, public Code API, audio/core/WASM/gains/defaults, SSF observer/ABI/renderer and package implementation remain byte-identical. Existing 206-case MAME native parity, eight-case SSF passive parity and historical source receipts are pinned unchanged; no new native or listening measurement is claimed",
